{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And they shall not die, neither they nor you.</b> From here we learn that the priests are not permitted to engage in the service of the Levites, nor the Levites in that of the priests, and even the priests and Levites themselves may not shift from one service to another, but as it is written (Numbers 4:15): ״איש על עבודתו״ — each man to his service, etc. And so they expounded in the Sifre: ״אך אל כלי הקדש ואל המזבח לא יקרבו״ — this is the warning; ״ולא ימותו״ — this is the punishment. From where do we know that the priests do not enter into the service of the Levites and the Levites into the service of the priests? Scripture says: ״גם הם״. From one service to its fellow, from where? Scripture says: ״גם אתם״. And indeed R. Joshua ben Chananiah sought to slam the doors shut, and Rabban Yochanan said to him: Go back behind you, for you are of the singers and you are not of the gatekeepers."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:33:41.872435685Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}